      "math_academy_id": "q-97027",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
